    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d251">

                <pb facs="0483" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Minister of Supply</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Beaverbrook</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Presidents Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d251-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-02">January 2,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Harry, You</hi> asked me to look into the
                    question of Cables &amp; Wireless Limited permitting transmissions by wireless
                    to Germany, Italy and Tokyo.</p>
                <p>I wrote to you yesterday telling you that I was expecting a cable from London on
                    the subject.</p>
                <p>I now send you a copy of the cable.</p>
                <p>I am unhappy to send you such a long telegram, but I am sending it just as I
                    received it.</p>
                <p>Yours ever,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Max</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d251-a1.xml" xpointer="d251-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
